## Sources

Where the data comes from, which commit / release is used and how the dictionary is derived from it.

## Installation

Make sure [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) is installed on your system and run

``` bash
uv sync
```

## Usage

``` bash
uv run build.py
```

This creates the dictionary in `out/` (`{{ repo_name }}.zip` + `{{ repo_name }}.index.json`).
Downloaded sources are cached in `tmp/sources/`, the uncompressed dictionary is kept in `tmp/{{ repo_name }}/` for inspection.

## Development

``` bash
uv run ruff check .          # lint
uv run ruff format .         # format
uv run pyright               # type check
uv run pytest                # tests
```

The repo follows the [DaLang dictionary repo standard](https://github.com/dariyooo/dalang-dict-utils/blob/main/docs/repo-standard.md),
update the shared setup with `uvx copier update --trust`.

## Release

Run the *Release* workflow from the Actions tab.
It runs the checks, builds the dictionary and publishes it as a GitHub release tagged with the date.
Installed dictionaries pick up new releases through "Check for updates".

